// Title: IIS WebServer Access Logs Deleted
// Sigma ID: 3eb8c339-a765-48cc-a150-4364c04652bf
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Tim Rauch (Nextron Systems), Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-09-16 | Modified: 2023-02-15
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1070
// Description: Detects the deletion of IIS WebServer access logs which may indicate an attempt to destroy
//   forensic evidence
// False positives:
//   - During uninstallation of the IIS service
//   - During log rotation
// References:
//   - https://www.elastic.co/guide/en/security/current/webserver-access-logs-deleted.html
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/file/file_delete/file_delete_win_delete_iis_access_logs.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceFileEvents
| where FolderPath contains "\\inetpub\\logs\\LogFiles\\" and FolderPath endswith ".log"
